#Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease

[[sk:COPD]]

{{rfc-case|[[chronic obstructive pulmonary disease]]}}
Broad descriptive term which identifies any disease processes of the lungs and chest that obstructs airflow. Caused by reactive airways, chronic infection, congenital defects and most commonly, cigerette smoking. Generally does not include neoplasams which could also obstruct airways.

Treatment includes reversing the obstruction by airway clearance techniques, medication to dilate the airways and removal of the irritant causing the obstruction. (most commonly smoking cessation)